Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Astro project

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies using pnpm
- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with new package and its dependencies

### 2. Updated Layout Component
- Modified `src/layouts/Layout.astro` to import Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/astro`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the HTML head section (before ClientRouter)

### 3. Verification Steps Completed
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors (astro check, astro build, pagefind)
- ✅ Linter passed with no errors
- ✅ All dependencies installed correctly
- ✅ Lock file (pnpm-lock.yaml) updated

## Implementation Details:

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Astro, I:
1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. Identified the Astro-specific implementation approach
3. Installed the @vercel/analytics package using pnpm (the project's package manager)
4. Added the Analytics component to the main Layout.astro file in the head section
5. The component will automatically inject the analytics tracking script

## Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
- `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `src/layouts/Layout.astro` - Added Analytics import and component

## Notes:
- The Analytics component is placed in the `<head>` section for optimal loading
- The component will automatically detect the environment (development/production)
- No additional configuration is needed; analytics will work once deployed to Vercel
- The implementation follows Astro best practices by using the framework-specific package entry point
